  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-17T14:07:31.399Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So, IK2 has been amazing for the most part but my biggest pet peeve so far and the only reason I cannot switch over permanently is the legs. \nI lay down a lot in VR and whenever I'm on the side with my knees together, the knees will never connect no matter how hard I try so it just leads to me awkwardly having my legs spread open at all times. \nFrom what I gather it is happening because the legs are not human proportionate. It's just frustrating since Legacy leg tracking never had this issue for me\n\nEdit:\nAfter trying again in the iterated Measure-by-arms in IK2 it seems to work better, but still not very natural. In measure-by-height I found it impossible to close them but with arm measure I can at least clench them together, though it isn't really a solution. \nIt just seems like the legs are fighting to not stay together. \n\nFirst is Legacy, Second is IK2 and I am using 6point tracking",
